From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_NX2_DMA_SNAPSHOT=1: macro DMA reads of flushed pages skip the back drain

Off unless set. Port of Frizti/Fritchii 8ac3666f7b + 28b262b59d + 526b9f240a (frizti-v3,
"Evil's DMA snapshot fix", EvilOOT's dma-snapshot fix, on by default there: Lake Hylia 46.5 ->
52.3 fps on PC, 0 differences in about 235,000 verified reads). Ocarina of Time reads an
occlusion report for each object (MME_DMA_READ_FIFOED, method 0x158), about 35,000 times a
second, and every read drained the split's back thread, so the front and the back took turns.
With the switch a drained read flushes its whole device pages (buffer cache) and remembers the
split position; a later read of those pages skips the drain while nothing sent since may write
them and the query cache lists no report there. =2 also drains, reads again and logs the first
32 differences (verify mode).

What the front tracks for this (new, all idle unless the switch is set):
- GpuSplit: NoteMemoryWrite(begin, size) ranges (4096-entry ring), NoteUnrangedWriter(),
  MayBeWrittenSince(since, begin, size): compute/copy sent since (NoteWriter), an unranged
  writer sent since, or a noted range that overlaps. Also NotedWriteSince() without the
  compute/copy test, for a later semaphore port.
- Maxwell3D front: report_semaphore.query (16 bytes at the report address), LAUNCH_DMA and
  inline_data (the upload's range; unranged when the address is unmapped or the completion
  releases a semaphore).
- DmaPusher: KeplerMemory and Fermi2D methods are unranged writers.
- Puller: semaphore releases (WriteLong, SemaphoreRelease, SEM_EXECUTE release) note 16 bytes
  at the semaphore (and its Switch 2 mirror); syncpoint increments are unranged.
- QueryCacheBase::HasCachedReports + RasterizerInterface/RasterizerVulkan::HasCachedReports:
  whether a report is still listed in the range (pending, or written and not unregistered).
Left out: Fritchii's known-words overlay (NoteMemoryWriteData), its Nx2Profile counters, the
Nx2CmdPageDiag and MACRO_DMA_DRAIN interplay, and the MSAA discard hunk that rode along in the
same commit. The existing path (Defer + Drain on every read, QueryDma hooks) is untouched when
the switch is unset, when QUERY_DMA_TRACE or QUERY_FLIP_TRACE is on, and for 0x157 reads.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/gpu_split.h b/src/video_core/gpu_split.h
index b67f742..34cebb9 100644
--- a/src/video_core/gpu_split.h
+++ b/src/video_core/gpu_split.h
@@ -181,6 +181,72 @@ public:
     /// Returns whether any of it was still queued.
     bool WaitForWriters();
 
+    // EDEN_NX2_DMA_SNAPSHOT (Frizti/Fritchii 8ac3666f7b, EvilOOT's dma-snapshot fix): the front
+    // notes the guest memory the work it sends may write, so a macro DMA read of a page a drained
+    // read flushed whole can tell whether anything sent since may have changed it.
+    /// Memory-writing work whose range the front does not know was just sent (KeplerMemory and
+    /// Fermi2D methods, syncpoint operations). Ends every macro DMA read snapshot.
+    void NoteUnrangedWriter() {
+        last_memory_writer_position = write_position;
+        last_unranged_position = write_position;
+    }
+    /// Work that writes the device range [begin, begin + size) was just sent (an inline upload, a
+    /// report, a semaphore release).
+    void NoteMemoryWrite(u64 begin, u64 size) {
+        last_memory_writer_position = write_position;
+        PendingWrite& write = pending_writes[pending_write_count++ % pending_writes.size()];
+        write.begin = begin;
+        write.end = begin + size;
+        write.position = write_position;
+    }
+    /// The ring position of everything sent so far.
+    [[nodiscard]] u64 SentPosition() const {
+        return write_position;
+    }
+    /// The back's position now: work at positions above it is still queued.
+    [[nodiscard]] u64 ConsumedNow() const {
+        return consumed.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
+    }
+    /// The last compute/copy and unranged writer positions.
+    [[nodiscard]] u64 LastWriterPosition() const {
+        return last_writer_position;
+    }
+    [[nodiscard]] u64 LastUnrangedPosition() const {
+        return last_unranged_position;
+    }
+    /// Whether work sent after position `since` may write device bytes [begin, begin + size):
+    /// compute or copies (any range), unranged writers, or a noted write that overlaps the range.
+    /// Also true when more writes were noted since than are remembered.
+    [[nodiscard]] bool MayBeWrittenSince(u64 since, u64 begin, u64 size) const {
+        if (last_writer_position > since || last_unranged_position > since) {
+            return true;
+        }
+        return NotedWriteSince(since, begin, size);
+    }
+    /// As MayBeWrittenSince without the compute and copy work: only the noted (ranged) writes and
+    /// the unranged writers. For a word on a page the GPU does not write (Nx2IsGpuWritten).
+    [[nodiscard]] bool NotedWriteSince(u64 since, u64 begin, u64 size) const {
+        if (last_unranged_position > since) {
+            return true;
+        }
+        if (last_memory_writer_position <= since) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        const u64 end = begin + size;
+        const u64 remembered = (std::min<u64>)(pending_write_count, pending_writes.size());
+        for (u64 scanned = 0; scanned < remembered; ++scanned) {
+            const PendingWrite& write =
+                pending_writes[(pending_write_count - 1 - scanned) % pending_writes.size()];
+            if (write.position <= since) {
+                return false;
+            }
+            if (write.begin < end && begin < write.end) {
+                return true;
+            }
+        }
+        return remembered == pending_writes.size();
+    }
+
 private:
     enum class Kind : u64 {
         Wrap,   ///< The rest of the ring is unused: continue at its start
@@ -247,6 +313,17 @@ private:
     // Front side.
     u64 write_position{};
     u64 last_writer_position{};
+    /// EDEN_NX2_DMA_SNAPSHOT: the positions of the last memory-writing work the front noted, and
+    /// the ranges of the last noted writes (NoteMemoryWrite), newest last.
+    u64 last_memory_writer_position{};
+    u64 last_unranged_position{};
+    struct PendingWrite {
+        u64 begin;
+        u64 end;
+        u64 position;
+    };
+    std::array<PendingWrite, 4096> pending_writes{};
+    u64 pending_write_count{};
     u64 published_local{};
     u64 consumed_cache{};
     /// Words between publishes: small right after a drain, while the back has nothing to do.
